# Line endings are declared by the repo, not by each machine's git config.
#
# Without this, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default) converts LF to CRLF
# on checkout, and every single `git add` prints
#   "warning: in the working copy of '<file>', LF will be replaced by CRLF"
# for every file it touches — pure noise that buries real warnings.
#
# LF everywhere: the repo already stores LF, this keeps the working copy the
# same so there is nothing to convert and nothing to warn about. It also stops
# line endings from depending on who checked the file out.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
